son &lt;brian.wilson@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="302062" owner_email="kevin.strasser@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/62/302062/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ia96a73ee4286b03294dcd089a42e3703f472a255" commit="dfd6d776f7f621b3403ba2d8e241607f2e5c3e15" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm/i915: split ibx_digital_port_connected to ibx and cpt variants  Choose the right function at the intel_digital_port_connected level.  Signed-off-by: Jani Nikula &lt;jani.nikula@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Durgadoss R &lt;durgadoss.r@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch&gt; LINK: http://anongit.freedesktop.org/git/drm-intel.git (cherry picked from commit 0df53b77287198502ff2eb51120c041ba317f059) Signed-off-by: Kevin Strasser &lt;kevin.strasser@intel.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44121 TEST=plug/unplug hdmi, check display status in ui  Change-Id: Ia96a73ee4286b03294dcd089a42e3703f472a255 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302063 Commit-Ready: Wayne Boyer &lt;wayne.boyer@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Brian Wilson &lt;brian.wilson@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="302063" owner_email="kevin.strasser@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/63/302063/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Iff032b7e31db3bfaa07f8c60f545682b3785e1f8" commit="b126887ae88bd8a22addc0a8052f37ca4be53866" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm/i915: split g4x_digital_port_connected to g4x and vlv variants  Choose the right function at the intel_digital_port_connected level.  Signed-off-by: Jani Nikula &lt;jani.nikula@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Durgadoss R &lt;durgadoss.r@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch&gt; LINK: http://anongit.freedesktop.org/git/drm-intel.git (cherry picked from commit 9642c81c225a43982536fcb7a3fa212dcfaa67ea) Signed-off-by: Kevin Strasser &lt;kevin.strasser@intel.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44121 TEST=plug/unplug hdmi, check display status in ui  Change-Id: Iff032b7e31db3bfaa07f8c60f545682b3785e1f8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302064 Commit-Ready: Wayne Boyer &lt;wayne.boyer@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Brian Wilson &lt;brian.wilson@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="302064" owner_email="kevin.strasser@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/64/302064/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ic0d0044ee1248caeb6b3d50c74b2013d8e4cf6a6" commit="559cbb662eb2cfd43936659b4780a3e55e59bbd1" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm/i915/bxt: Use correct live status register for BXT platform  BXT platform uses live status bits from 0x44440 register to obtain DP status on hotplug. The existing g4x_digital_port_connected() uses a different register and hence misses DP hotplug events on BXT platform. This patch fixes it by using the appropriate register(0x44440) and live status bits(3:5).  Based on a patch by Durgadoss R &lt;durgadoss.r@intel.com&gt;, from whom the commit message is shamelessly copy pasted.  Reported-by: Durgadoss R &lt;durgadoss.r@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Jani Nikula &lt;jani.nikula@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Durgadoss R &lt;durgadoss.r@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch&gt; LINK: http://anongit.freedesktop.org/git/drm-intel.git (cherry picked from commit e464bfdeda3da3b0ef29ca84960715993ccbb1fc) Signed-off-by: Kevin Strasser &lt;kevin.strasser@intel.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44121 TEST=plug/unplug hdmi, check display status in ui  Change-Id: Ic0d0044ee1248caeb6b3d50c74b2013d8e4cf6a6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302065 Commit-Ready: Wayne Boyer &lt;wayne.boyer@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Brian Wilson &lt;brian.wilson@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="302065" owner_email="kevin.strasser@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/65/302065/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I5fa2c1cca1df1ad7a0f1d67cd7df6a1f7b324c30" commit="07413ee134265c845d0520abdc70e6015273f25a" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm/i915: add attached connector to hdmi container  This patch adds the intel_connector initialized to intel_hdmi display, during the init phase, just like the other encoders do. This attachment is very useful when we need to extract the connector pointer during the hotplug handler function  Signed-off-by: Shashank Sharma &lt;shashank.sharma@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Rodrigo Vivi &lt;rodrigo.vivi@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch&gt; LINK: http://anongit.freedesktop.org/git/drm-intel.git (cherry picked from commit d8b4c43a4baccecee7106c1432baa986fab9593a) Signed-off-by: Kevin Strasser &lt;kevin.strasser@intel.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44121 TEST=plug/unplug hdmi, check display status in ui  Change-Id: I5fa2c1cca1df1ad7a0f1d67cd7df6a1f7b324c30 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302066 Commit-Ready: Wayne Boyer &lt;wayne.boyer@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Brian Wilson &lt;brian.wilson@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="302066" owner_email="kevin.strasser@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/66/302066/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I612d80c844c39e3e1157a1ee8afe30896c53f399" commit="034f7f71ffd901dd9331f91f5d9a0da9e1397be9" commit_message="BACKPORT: drm/i915: Check live status before reading edid  The Bspec is very clear that Live status must be checked about before trying to read EDID over DDC channel. This patch makes sure that HDMI EDID is read only when live status is up.  The live status doesn't seem to perform very consistent across various platforms when tested with different monitors. The reason behind that is some monitors are late to provide right voltage to set live_status up. So, after getting the interrupt, for a small duration, live status reg fluctuates, and then settles down showing the correct staus.  This is explained here in, in a rough way: HPD line  ________________     |\ T1 = Monitor Hotplug causing IRQ     | \______________________________________     | |                          | |     | |   T2 = Live status is stable     | |  _____________________________________     | | /| Live status _____________|_|/ |     | |  |     | |  |     | |  |    T0 T1  T2  (Between T1 and T2 Live status fluctuates or can be even low, depending on  the monitor)  After several experiments, we have concluded that a max delay of 30ms is enough to allow the live status to settle down with most of the monitors. This total delay of 30ms has been split into a resolution of 3 retries of 10ms each, for the better cases.  This delay is kept at 30ms, keeping in consideration that, HDCP compliance expect the HPD handler to respond a plug out in 100ms, by disabling port.  v2: Adding checks for VLV/CHV as well. Reusing old ibx and g4x functions to check digital port status. Adding a separate function to get bxt live status (Daniel) v3: Using intel_encoder-&gt;hpd_pin to check the live status (Siva) Moving the live status read to intel_hdmi_probe and passing parameter to read/not to read the edid. (me) v4: * Added live status check for all platforms using intel_digital_port_connected. * Rebased on top of Jani's DP cleanup series * Some monitors take time in setting the live status. So retry for few times if this is a connect HPD v5: Removed extra &quot;drm/i915&quot; from commit message. Adding Shashank's sob     which was missed. v6: Drop the (!detect_edid &amp;&amp; !live_status check) check because for DDI ports which are enumerated as hdmi as well as DP, we don't have a mechanism to differentiate between DP and hdmi inside the encoder's hot_plug. This leads to call to the hdmi's hot_plug hook for DP as well as hdmi which leads to issues during unplug because of the above check. v7: Make intel_digital_port_connected global in this patch, some reformatting of while loop, adding a print when live status is not up. (Rodrigo) v8: Rebase it on nightly which involved skipping the hot_plug hook for now and letting the live_status check happen in detect until the hpd handling part is finalized (Daniel)  Signed-off-by: Shashank Sharma &lt;shashank.sharma@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Sonika Jindal &lt;sonika.jindal@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Rodrigo Vivi &lt;rodrigo.vivi@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch&gt; LINK: http://anongit.freedesktop.org/git/drm-intel.git (cherry picked from commit 237ed86c693d8a8e4db476976aeb30df4deac74b) [strassek: fix trivial merge conflict] Signed-off-by: Kevin Strasser &lt;kevin.strasser@intel.com&gt;  Conflicts:  drivers/gpu/drm/i915/intel_drv.h  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44121 TEST=plug/unplug hdmi, check display status in ui  Change-Id: I612d80c844c39e3e1157a1ee8afe30896c53f399 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302067 Commit-Ready: Wayne Boyer &lt;wayne.boyer@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Brian Wilson &lt;brian.wilson@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="302067" owner_email="kevin.strasser@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/67/302067/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic4e4406e41a401d7d4200e4be7069baae7d22be4" commit="259ae3dc150f6886b42ec9acf4d9a190ba47ee8d" commit_message="build_stages.py: change to always run SetupBoard cmd  The SetupBoard cmds get ran only when the board is not there or config to replace the board. However, CQ gets 'Cannot find prebuilts for chromos-base/chromeos-chrome because' builder doesn't update its prebuilts using setup_board when chrome is updated. For the stability of CQ, change to always run the SetupBoard cmd.  BUG=chromium:509150 TEST=unittest and trybot.  Change-Id: Ic4e4406e41a401d7d4200e4be7069baae7d22be4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303154 Commit-Ready: Shuqian Zhao &lt;shuqianz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shuqian Zhao &lt;shuqianz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David James &lt;davidjames@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="303154" owner_email="shuqianz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/54/303154/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><lkgm version="7511.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>